      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Despite several attempts, balloon angioplasty of a slightly eccentric stenotic lesion in the proximal right coronary artery failed to result in any increase of luminal diameter. Following disruption and partial removal of a fibrous atherosclerotic cap using directional atherectomy, subsequent balloon angioplasty was highly successful."},
